
== the largest and smallest values ==
9223372036854775807d (max mantissa)          9223372036854775807
-9223372036854775807d                        -9223372036854775807
92233720368547758.07d (scale 2)              92233720368547758.07
0.9223372036854775807d (scale 19)            0.9223372036854775807
0.0000000000000000000000000001d (scale 28)   0.0000000000000000000000000001
9.223372036854775807d                        9.223372036854775807

== literals that do not fit are syntax errors ==
return 9223372036854775808d                  Decimal literal is out of range
return 92233720368547758070d                 Decimal literal is out of range
return 1e19d                                 Decimal literal is out of range
return 1e30d                                 Decimal literal is out of range
return 0.00000000000000000000000000001d      Decimal literal is out of range
return 1e-29d                                Decimal literal is out of range
return 1.2.3d                                Malformed decimal
return 1ed                                   Malformed decimal

== a result with too many digits is rounded, the scale drops ==
92233720368547758.07d + 0.01d                92233720368547758.1
92233720368547758.07d + 0.001d               92233720368547758.07
92233720368547758.07d + 0.1d                 92233720368547758.2
0.1234567890123456789d * 1d                  0.1234567890123456789
0.1234567890123456789d * 0.1234567890123456789d 0.01524157875323883675
9223372036854775.807d * 1.5d                 13835058055282163.71
1d / 3d * 3d                                 1.000000000000000000

== the scale is capped at 28 ==
0.0000000000000001d * 0.0000000000000001d    0.0000000000000000000000000000
0.0000000000000001d * 0.00000000000000001d   0.0000000000000000000000000000
0.0000000000000001d * 0.000000000000000001d  0.0000000000000000000000000000
1d / 9223372036854775807d                    0.0000000000000000001084202172
decimal.create(1e-29)                        0.0000000000000000000000000000

== overflow: a value that does not fit even at scale 0 ==
9223372036854775807d + 1d                    error: decimal overflow
9223372036854775807d * 2d                    error: decimal overflow
9223372036854775807d * 10d                   error: decimal overflow
-9223372036854775807d - 2d                   error: decimal overflow
1000000000d * 1000000000d * 100d             error: decimal overflow
decimal.mul(5000000000d, 5000000000d)        error: decimal overflow
1000000000d * 1000000000d (fits)             1000000000000000000
99999999999999999d + 1d (fits)               100000000000000000

== but digits can be traded for range ==
922337203685477580.7d + 0.1d                 922337203685477581
922337203685477580.7d * 10d                  9223372036854775807
922337203685477580.7d * 100d                 error: decimal overflow

== remainder has its own limit: both operands scaled to a common scale ==
1d % 0.0000000000000000001d                  0.0000000000000000000
9223372036854775807d % 0.0000000000000000000000001d error: decimal overflow

== what 63 bits are good for ==
largest amount with 2 decimals               92233720368547758.07
largest amount with 4 decimals               922337203685477.5807
largest amount with 8 decimals               92233720368.54775807
largest amount with 18 decimals              9.223372036854775807
